{"The test monkeypatches time.sleep to a no-op, so the new time.sleep(0.1) call never actually yields to the flusher processes, causing the test to still race on slow machines because nothing waits after bumping current_drift": 0.8293049931526184, "The call to record_stored_segments() iterates over self.buffers which only contains per-process shard buffers that never receive process_spans calls, causing the real buffer's recently_stored_segments counters to never be drained, spans.buffer.* metrics to remain at zero, and the bookkeeping list to grow without bound": 0.8739434480667114, "Setting default=1 on the --flusher-processes option means the strategy factory always passes flusher_processes=1, so the per-shard multiprocessing logic is never exercised unless operators explicitly override the flag, defeating the goal of spawning one process per shard": 0.9348720908164978}